  "description": "This Building Block proposes a schema representation of the OpenEO process [`pi`](https://processes.openeo.org/#pi) \u2014 *Pi (\u03c0)*. It models the `arguments` object of a process graph node invoking `pi`. This is a proposed correspondence between the OpenEO process definition and an OGC Building Block schema, not a settled equivalence.\n\nThe real number Pi (\u03c0) is a mathematical constant that is the ratio of the circumference of a circle to its diameter. The numerical value is approximately *3.14159*.\n\n## Source\n\nOpenEO Processes specification: [`pi`](https://processes.openeo.org/#pi) ([openeo-processes/pi.json at 2.0.0-rc.2](https://github.com/Open-EO/openeo-processes/blob/2.0.0-rc.2/pi.json)).\n",
